  (use "git add <file>..." to update what will be committed)
  (use "git restore <file>..." to discard changes in working directory)
        modified:   libdm/datastruct/bitset.c
        modified:   libdm/ioctl/libdm-iface.c
        modified:   libdm/libdm-deptree.c




All the changes that are made in the effort to build a dynamic library for Linux are made on top of the 5.17.0 tag.
Here are the steps involving git:
(1). git clone the original project (not the forked)
(2). checkout a particular tag 5.17.0 (commit hash starts with 1ab05a6e4)
     In order to not make the local repository a "head detached" state, I created a new local branch "release/5.17.0"
(3). make source code and CMake file changes
(4). set the remote url to my fork (git remote set-url https://github.com/yuekunli/osquery.git)
(5). create yet another branch (I'm currently on release/5.17.0, created dev/5.17.0/dll-linux on top of release/5.17.0)
(6). commit changes locally
(7). push changes to remote (my fork)



commit 1ab05a6e4a21b8a6b6531ed45ecc4a748b47f5d1 (HEAD -> dev/5.17.0/dll-linux, tag: 5.17.0, release/5.17.0)
Author: Jaymz Julian <jaymz@artificial-stupidity.net>
Date:   Tue Apr 15 21:56:17 2025 -0700

    Filter the Win32_Processor query to only required fields (#8598)

    Querying Win32_Processor for all fields has a performance penalty of 1.1s per CPU core - this is mostly unnoticable on small boxes, but on larger boxes can actualloy have a significant impact on startup performance.  Even on an 8 core system, this takes the startup time for osqueryi from 8.5s to 0.2s.
